⍝ bench/scout/engines/dyalog.apls - Dyalog APL side of the scout matrix (core tier).
⍝ Run:  dyalogscript bench/scout/engines/dyalog.apls <op> <N> <runs> <warmup>
⍝ Protocol and data model: bench/scout/SCOUT_SPEC.md
⍝
⍝ ⎕IO←0 so indices are 0-based like every other engine.  Core tier only (no
⍝ table layer).  Dyalog squeezes every integral array to its narrowest type,
⍝ so x and y are STORED as int16 however they are built (the CBQN note applies);
⍝ values past 2^31 become float64, so every sum below stays exact.
⍝ Idioms: {⍵[⍋⍵]} sort, dyadic ⍳ / ∊ / monadic ∪ (hashed), X+.×Y dot product,
⍝ the key operator ⌸ for group-by (keys in first-appearance order), and n-wise
⍝ reduction for the moving windows (16+/ over a vector padded with the identity
⍝ of + so the first windows are partial; 64⌈/ padded with ⌈/⍬ likewise).
⍝ Timing: 10⎕DT'Z' is the current time in nanoseconds (exact, decimal float).
⍝ Output: in script mode ⎕← ends its lines with a bare CR (a line-oriented
⍝ reader does not split on it) and ⍞← goes to stderr, so the protocol lines are
⍝ appended to /dev/stdout through a native tie, each ended by an explicit LF.
⍝ The workspace cap (MAXWS) is raised by the dyalogscript wrapper, not here.

⎕IO←0
⎕PP←17
NL←⎕UCS 10
⍝ single thread: 1111⌶ is the thread count Dyalog may use to run scalar
⍝ functions on large arrays in parallel (it defaults to the number of cores)
PREV_THREADS←1111⌶1

ARGS←¯4↑2⎕NQ#'GetCommandLineArgs'
OP←0⊃ARGS
N←⍎1⊃ARGS
RUNS←⍎2⊃ARGS
WARM←⍎3⊃ARGS

I←⍳N
H←⌊1048573|262147×I
A←1000|H
B←997|H
X←A+0.0
Y←B+0.0
CHK←(+/A)+3×+/B

KR←1048573|7919×⍳1000
VR←2×⍳1000
MJ←1000000

SFA←{m←≢⍵ ⋄ (+/⍵[0,(⌊m÷4),(⌊m÷2),(⌊3×m÷4),m-1])+1E9×+/(1↓⍵)<¯1↓⍵}
DSUM←{(1E6×≢⍵)++/⍵}
GRP←{r←⍺{⍺,+/⍵}⌸⍵ ⋄ +/(1+251|r[;0])×r[;1]}

OPS←'sum_f' 'max_f' 'scan_f' 'dot' 'sum_i' 'arith_mask'
OPS,←'sort_f' 'sort_presorted' 'grade_i' 'find' 'member'
OPS,←'distinct' 'distinct_100k' 'group_10' 'group_100' 'group_10k' 'group_100k'
OPS,←'join_inner' 'msum_16' 'mavg_256' 'mmax_64'

SETUPS←'NOP←0' 'NOP←0' 'NOP←0' 'NOP←0' 'NOP←0' 'NOP←0'
SETUPS,←'NOP←0' 'P←X[⍋X]' 'GK←1000⌊N' 'PR←KR[1000|H]' 'NOP←0'
SETUPS,←'NOP←0' 'G5←100000|H' 'G←10|H' 'G←100|H' 'G←10000|H' 'G←100000|H'
SETUPS,←⊂'HJ←⌊1048573|262147×⍳MJ ⋄ KL←KR[1000|HJ] ⋄ VL←1000|HJ'
SETUPS,←'NOP←0' 'NOP←0' 'NOP←0'

KERNS←'{+/X}' '{⌈/X}' '{S←+\X ⋄ S[0]+S[⌊N÷2]+S[N-1]}' '{X+.×Y}' '{+/A}' '{+/(X>50)/Y+2.5×X}'
KERNS,←'{SFA X[⍋X]}' '{SFA P[⍋P]}' '{+/GK↑⍋A}' '{+/KR⍳PR}' '{+/H∊KR}'
KERNS,←'{DSUM ∪A}' '{DSUM ∪G5}' '{G GRP X}' '{G GRP X}' '{G GRP X}' '{G GRP X}'
KERNS,←'{+/VL×VR[KR⍳KL]}' '{+/16+/(15⍴0),X}' '{+/(256+/(255⍴0),X)÷256⌊1+⍳N}' '{+/64⌈/(63⍴⌈/⍬),X}'

∇ OUT LINE;T
  T←'/dev/stdout'⎕NTIE 0
  (LINE,NL)⎕NAPPEND T 80
  ⎕NUNTIE T
∇

∇ MAIN;J;TS;ANS;T0;R
  J←OPS⍳⊂OP
  :If J=≢OPS
      OUT'SKIP ',OP
      :Return
  :EndIf
  ⍎J⊃SETUPS
  ⍎'KF←',J⊃KERNS
  ANS←0
  :For R :In ⍳WARM
      ANS←KF 0
  :EndFor
  TS←⍬
  :For R :In ⍳RUNS
      T0←10⎕DT'Z'
      ANS←KF 0
      TS,←((10⎕DT'Z')-T0)÷1000000
  :EndFor
  OUT'BENCH   ',OP
  OUT'CHECK   ',⍕CHK
  OUT'ANSWER  ',⍕ANS
  OUT'TIME_MS ',⍕(TS[⍋TS])[⌊RUNS÷2]
∇

MAIN
⎕OFF
